(vector (map (:db/id -1) (:adr/id 2799007121) (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7121 \u2014 Roofers Job-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage") (:adr/status "accepted") (:adr/doc_type "adr") (:adr/date "2026-07-17") (:adr/source-format "edn") (:adr/scope (vector "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121" "kotoba-lang/occupation")) (:adr/references (vector 2607121000 2607152500)) (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2607152500-cloud-itonami-wave4-rollout-start-amendment")) (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)) (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)) (:registry/maturity :implemented) (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7121") (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121") (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7121) (:actor/name "Roofing Crew Scheduling & Logistics Coordination Service") (:actor/isco-08 "7121") (:actor/wave 3) (:actor/domain :construction/roofing-coordination) (:actor/robotics? true) (:actor/coordination? true) (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)) (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-site :no-actuation :unknown-op :site-mismatch :unknown-worker :worker-wrong-site :scope-exclusion-violation)) (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)) (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-roof-work-execution :execute-roof-work-directly :perform-roofing-work-directly :override-fall-protection-judgment :override-site-safety-officer :bypass-safety-officer-signoff)) (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the roof-work" "proceed with the roofing work" "finalize the roof-work-execution decision" "finalize the roofing-work-execution decision" "execute the roof-work directly" "execute the roofing work directly" "perform the roofing work directly" "dispatch the crew to perform roofing work" "override the fall-protection safety judgment" "override the site-safety officer" "override the safety officer's fall-protection judgment" "bypass the fall-protection safety judgment" "bypass the site-safety officer" "bypass fall-protection sign-off")) (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 10000}") (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)) (:operation/entry-point :intake) (:test/simulator :roofcoord.actor-test) (:test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 52, :failures 0, :errors 0}") (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :site-verification :worker-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :always-escalate-safety-concern)) (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007121: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7121 Roofers job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7121\n-- Roofers** only. The occupation-actor track is currently working\nWave3 (production/trades); ISCO Wave0/Wave1 are both 100% complete.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7121\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7121\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Roofers\" -- confirming the\npremise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was\n`:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]`, `:optional-technologies []` and `:operating-states\n[:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit]`, and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7121` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**This actor carries a height-work safety dimension: roofers work at\nheight on active job sites, one of the highest fall-risk trades.** A\nwrongful automated decision here could directly endanger a worker's\nlife. The closed op allowlist therefore must NEVER include any op that\ndirectly finalizes a roofing-work-execution decision or overrides a\nsite-safety officer's fall-protection judgment -- such a decision must\nalways be a hard, permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This is the same underlying principle the\nWave4-amendment ADR (ADR-2607152500) established for decisions directly\ntouching safety, dignity or subsistence in the human-services track:\nthe capability to finalize such a decision must be structurally\nexcluded from the closed op allowlist, not merely gated behind\nescalation. This actor applies that same shape to the fall-protection\nsafety dimension, even though roofers is a Wave3 (production/trades)\noccupation, because a worker's physical safety at height carries the\nsame weight as the decision classes that precedent protects.\n\n**This actor coordinates JOB-SITE SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it never\nperforms roofing work itself.** It is not an authority to decide when\nor how roofing work happens on a roof; it is a coordination layer for\nwork-record logging, crew scheduling, safety-concern surfacing and\nmaterials-order coordination, all gated behind an independent\ngovernor.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set: README,\nCODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, LICENSE\n(AGPL-3.0-or-later), SECURITY.md, docs/business-model.md,\ndocs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn), cloned and read in full this\nsession.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121` as an OSS\ndocumentation/coordination actor for roofers, following the same\ngoverned-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Roof Coordination Advisor \u22a3 RoofCoordGovernor**\non a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger. All source is portable `.cljc` (no JVM interop); tests\nare `clojure.test` `.clj`, matching the reference repo's own layout.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a fall-hazard/weather-condition/\n  crew-fatigue concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- roofing-materials procurement\n  proposal, escalates above a registered cost threshold\n\nNo op in this allowlist finalizes a roofing-work-execution decision or\noverrides a site-safety officer's fall-protection judgment -- these\ndecision classes are structurally absent from the allowlist, not\nmerely gated behind escalation.\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (`roofcoord.governor`, permanent, never\noverridable by human approval)\n\n1. **no-site** -- the job site named by the request must be\n   independently verified/registered before any action.\n2. **no-actuation** -- proposal `:effect` must be `:propose` (the\n   governor never dispatches hardware and never performs roofing\n   work).\n3. **unknown-op** -- `:op` must be one of the four allowlisted\n   coordination ops; the closed op-allowlist is enforced\n   unconditionally.\n4. **site-mismatch** -- if the proposal names a site, it must be the\n   SAME site verified for this request (defense-in-depth against a\n   proposal quietly targeting an unverified site).\n5. **unknown-worker / worker-wrong-site** -- if the proposal\n   references a worker, that worker must be a REGISTERED crew member\n   belonging to this site.\n6. **scope-exclusion-violation** -- a proposal that attempts, in any\n   free-text field, to finalize a roofing-work-execution decision or\n   to override a site-safety officer's fall-protection judgment is a\n   HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated unconditionally on content,\n   independent of `:op`.\n\n### Escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`roofcoord.governor/always-escalate-ops`). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a fall-hazard/\n  weather-condition/crew-fatigue observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (10000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-or-below-cost-threshold`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence.\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates,\n  for any op.\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare nouns (e.g.\n\"roof\", \"height\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's own\ndefault rationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the\nactor's own happy path -- this risk is especially sharp here because\nthis actor's ENTIRE domain is roofing job sites at height, so bare\nnouns like \"roof\"/\"height\" are ordinary, unavoidable vocabulary.\n`roofcoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTION PHRASES (e.g. \"proceed with the\nroof-work\", \"override the fall-protection safety judgment\", \"override\nthe site-safety officer\"), never bare nouns, and\n`roofcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor (including a\n`:flag-safety-concern` request whose description names a fall hazard\n\"near the roof edge at height\"), never trips the scope-exclusion\nguard. A companion test,\n`scope-exclusion-not-triggered-by-bare-domain-nouns`, asserts directly\nagainst `governor/scope-exclusion-violation?` that a rationale/\ndescription containing only bare domain nouns (\"roof job site ... at\nheight ... fall-protection equipment for this roof\") does not trip the\nguard, while `hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-roof-work`\nand `hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-safety-officer`\nconfirm the actual forbidden action phrases DO trip it, and\n`holds-a-scope-excluded-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path` confirms the\nfull actor graph resolves such an attempt straight to `:hold` (a\nfinish point, never `:request-approval`) with no record committed.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7121\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7121`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 52 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a fresh clone of the pushed repository.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-3313`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-roof-work-completion` that is\n  merely gated behind `always-escalate-ops` (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit height-work-safety\n  guidance and the `ADR-2607152500` precedent -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a roofing-work-execution\n  decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human\n  gate. For a decision that can directly endanger a worker's life at\n  height, the capability itself must not exist in the allowlist at\n  all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"roof\" \"height\"]`):\n  rejected per the fleet-known self-trip bug class -- this actor's\n  entire domain is roofing job sites at height, so bare nouns would\n  self-trip on essentially every legitimate proposal (materials\n  orders naming \"roofing shingles\", safety flags naming a hazard \"at\n  height\", etc.).\n- Checking site/worker provenance only from the proposal (never the\n  request): rejected -- the site-mismatch check requires the site\n  identity to be anchored at the request level and independently\n  cross-checked against anything the proposal claims, so a proposal\n  that quietly names a different, unverified site is caught even if\n  the proposal otherwise looks well-formed.\n- Modeling the worker-registration check as unconditionally required\n  on every op: rejected as too rigid -- `:coordinate-supply-order`\n  legitimately has no worker to reference (it is a materials-\n  procurement proposal against the site, not a person); the check\n  applies only when a proposal actually references a `:worker-id`.\n")))
